{
 "result": "My body is maze.py: it reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a one-cell wall border in a single flat bytearray, and runs a level-synchronous BFS from S with the visited map pre-marked from the walls. Each level is expanded with four unrolled neighbour checks, and E is tested when a cell is first reached. It prints the distance, or -1 if E is unreachable or S or E is missing. It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) and was assayed at a median of 4.02 (noise 5.4%), a +42% gain on the original baseline. Further tweaks I tried were not adopted, so I am stopping here.",
